     men_of_arms line. P.P.E. P.E. + 2D6x10 + 2D6 per level. I.S.P. M.E. +
     1D4x10 + 1D6 per level (the two strings differ, as printed).
  3. PSIONICS: minor psionic, four powers from Healing or Physical, as printed
     (four, not the two a minor psionic usually gets). No per-level powers.
  4. MAGIC: four spells from levels 1-3 at level one, one more per level after
     that, never above the character''s level. General invocations only - no
     tradition.
  5. BONUSES: +1 initiative, +2 strike, +1 parry, +1 dodge, +1 pull punch, +1
     roll with impact, +1 save vs magic (spell_magic) and psionics, +5 save vs
     horror factor. All unconditional. No attacks-per-melee figure is printed,
     so no attacks_base.
  6. SKILLS. Basic Math is Mathematics: Basic 45+15. Ancient Egyptian (+20%)
     has no catalog row and is a fixed Language: Other at 50+20, the tongue
     named in the note. Dragonese/Elf (+15%) is Language: Dragonese 50+15.
     One language of choice +15% is a Language: Other pick. Track Animals is
     Track & Trap Animals 20+20; Track Humans/Monsters is Tracking (people)
     25+15; Wilderness Survival 30+20; Detect Ambush 30+10; Swim is Swimming
     50+10. No literacy is printed and none was added.
  7. HAND TO HAND: the book prints Hand to Hand: Expert twice (once bare, once
     with the upgrade note) - read as one grant. Expert changes to Martial Arts
     for one other skill: hand_to_hand costs martial_arts 1. No Assassin option
     is printed, so none is offered.
  8. RELATED SKILLS. This R.C.C. prints its own "other" skill package and
     pairs with no O.C.C., so they are stored as occ_related_skills, as the
     Amazon R.C.C. from the same book was: five plus one at levels 3, 5, 7, 11
     and 15. Domestic, Espionage, Technical and Wilderness +10%, Pilot +5%;
     Medical First Aid and Holistic Medicine only; Military and Science none.
  9. SECONDARY: five, from the same list without the bonuses. "An additional
     two skills at levels three, eight, and twelve" is read as two at EACH of
     those levels, the reading the Sailor and Pirate drafts from this book
     took for the same phrasing. If it means one each, the schedule counts
     become 1.
  10. EQUIPMENT: the enchanted plate armor (100 M.D.C.) is the Manoan Enchanted
      Plate Armor row, the only enchanted M.D.C. plate from this book (the
      Sekhmet live in Omagua, not Manoa; the item is the closest catalog row).
      The techno-wizard or energy weapon is a choice from a catalog set led by
      this book''s own weapons. Survival gear is survival-kit, food is one
      food-rations, the cloak is hooded-cloak; the loincloth has no row and is
      prose.
  11. MONEY: 1D6x1000 in salable items is not coin, so starting_money is not
      stored; it is a restriction line.
  12. Horror Factor 12 is stored in horror_factor and repeated as a
      restriction line.
