# Sekhmet

## Lore

The Sekhmet, or Children of Sekhmet, take their name from an Egyptian feline goddess, sister of Bast, who is said to have created or found their race. They are lion-headed humanoids with a lion''s tail, somewhat like the Ramen of Rifts Africa but smaller, and have served many feline gods, among them the African lion-god Simba.

They are a race of warrior-hunters who travel in war bands of a dozen to a hundred, split into prides of four to six. The bands live semi-nomadically, hunting off the land or hiring out as mercenaries, and in some places raiding. Children learn to fight and track as soon as they can walk, and harsh initiation rites - the Coming of Age, the Time of the Warrior and, for a few, the Time of Choosing that makes a Pride Leader - weed out the weak. The Coming of Age also opens a link to the supernatural through which a sekhmet learns magic by instinct.

The Children of Sekhmet have fought in divine wars across the Megaverse against demons, devils, gargoyles, vampires, the Splugorth, True Atlanteans, Ramen, Tautons and many others.

## GM Notes

Simba has declared Omagua a safe haven for all sekhmet. Over 50,000 live there permanently and thousands more pass through; most serve the Pantheons of Light or seek heroic adventure, and they have learned to respect the city''s werebeasts and mutant felinoids. Mixed war bands or prides of several feline races, mortal and superhuman, are common, and the book suggests such a group - possibly all player characters - sent on missions by Omagua or by Simba as a campaign focus.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'sekhmet');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'sekhmet';

